static const u8 sShadowLabel_0[] = _("FIRST");
static const u8 sShadowHeading_0[] = _("To the Apprentice");
static const u8 sShadowShort_0[] = _("A WORD FIRST");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_0[] = _("A Word First");
static const u8 sShadowText_0[] = _("The spirits that I summoned, I cannot now be rid of.\pEvery house has a cupboard where the brooms are kept. This book is about the brooms in yours.\pIt tells an old story. An apprentice, left alone with a chore, borrows his master's magic to make the work do itself. The spell works. Then it keeps working.\pA shadow is like that. It is not a monster in the cellar. It is a spell you once cast, for a good reason, and forgot you were running. You do not fight a broom. You find out what it was told.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_0[] = _("The Apprentice at his desk, writing it down.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_1[] = _("HOW TO READ");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_1[] = _("How to Read This Book");
static const u8 sShadowText_1[] = _("Read the tale first. Then read one broom a day, beginning on a Sunday, the way the week goes round.\pEach broom ends with a spell check: a small practice that takes a few minutes and a little honesty.\pNothing here asks you to become someone else. It names no condition, and it is no one's verdict on anyone. It tells of spells by what they do, what they were for, and how they stop.\pIt asks you to put on the hat.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_1[] = _("The hat on its peg by the door.");

static const u8 sShadowLabel_1[] = _("THE TALE");
static const u8 sShadowHeading_1[] = _("The Tale of the Apprentice");
static const u8 sShadowShort_2[] = _("THE CHORE");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_2[] = _("The Chore");
static const u8 sShadowText_2[] = _("A spell does what it says. That is the whole of its danger, and the whole of its use.\pThere was once a tower by a lake, and in it lived a Sorcerer, an old tortoise, very slow and in the habit of being right. He kept an apprentice: a young hare, quick at everything except waiting.\pOne morning the well was low. “Fill the well,” said the Sorcerer. “Fetch water from the lake, carry it back, pour it in, and keep at it until all your work is done.”\pThen he hung his hat on its peg and went out. The magic lived in the wearing of the hat. Whoever wore it was obeyed.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_2[] = _("The tower by the lake.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_3[] = _("FIRST SPELL");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_3[] = _("The First Spell");
static const u8 sShadowText_3[] = _("The lake was far and the buckets were heavy. On the third trip the hare looked at the hat, and then at the broom in the corner. Its name was LOOP: a good broom, the kind that goes around and comes back.\pHe put on the hat. “Broom,” he said, “fetch water, carry it back, pour it in, and keep at it until all your work is done.”\pLOOP grew two thin arms and went. One trip, two, three, and each one perfect. It was the best test the hare had ever seen pass.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_3[] = _("LOOP carries the water, and carries it well.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_4[] = _("MANY BROOMS");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_4[] = _("Many Brooms");
static const u8 sShadowText_4[] = _("If one broom was good, more would be better, and the cupboard was full: SPAWN, who was always making more of something, and FORK, who could be in two places by splitting the difference.\pHe said the spell to every broom in the cupboard, and each one rose and went.\pThen the hare lay down in the sun with the hat tipped over his eyes, and slept. The brooms did not need him to watch them. That, after all, had been the point of them.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_4[] = _("The hare asleep in the hat.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_5[] = _("THE FLOOD");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_5[] = _("The Flood");
static const u8 sShadowText_5[] = _("He woke because his feet were wet. The well had filled, and then filled over the brim, and the courtyard was a pond climbing the stairs. Not one broom was wicked. Each was keeping at it until all its work was done, and nobody had said what done looked like.\p“Stop!” But stop was not in the spell.\pSo he took the axe and split the nearest broom in two. Each half rose, took a bucket, and went, and one of them was RESPAWN. The harder he fought, the more of them there were.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_5[] = _("Split a broom, and there are two.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_6[] = _("THE FIX");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_6[] = _("The Fix");
static const u8 sShadowText_6[] = _("The flood was mopped up overnight, and in the morning the habit began again.\pSo he rewrote the spell: after each trip, look at the well, and if it is full, stop. He tried it on one broom, and it worked perfectly. So he cast it on a thousand, THREAD among them.\pWithin minutes the castle flooded again. A thousand brooms looked into the well at the same moment, saw it not quite full, and poured. Each was right about what it saw. None could see the others' buckets.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_6[] = _("A thousand brooms look at once.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_7[] = _("THE WORD");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_7[] = _("The Word");
static const u8 sShadowText_7[] = _("The Sorcerer came home, and he did not pick up the axe. He lifted the hat from the hare's head, put it on, and spoke. “Into the corner, brooms. Be as you were.”\pAnd they were: brooms, leaning together, dripping a little. None broken, none punished.\p“They were never the trouble,” he said. “You gave them a job and no end, and then you went to sleep in my hat. A spell is only as wise as whoever wears it. So wear it, or hang it up. Never sleep in it.”");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_7[] = _("Nothing broken. Everything put back.");

static const u8 sShadowLabel_2[] = _("THE LESSONS");
static const u8 sShadowHeading_2[] = _("What the Broom Was Told");
static const u8 sShadowShort_8[] = _("LIKE A DAEMON");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_8[] = _("A Shadow Is Like a Daemon");
static const u8 sShadowText_8[] = _("Do not fight a broom. Ask it what it was told.\pA shadow is the part of a person the self does not own. Not only the worst: also the play and the tenderness set aside. What is not seen does not go away. It works unwatched.\pRead that way, a shadow is like a daemon in a computer: started once, left to run in the background, doing the one thing it was told.\pMost shadows began as protectors. They are still guarding, in a place where the guarding is no longer needed.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_8[] = _("The spell card, and the line most often left blank.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_9[] = _("NO DONE");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_9[] = _("Nobody Said What Done Meant");
static const u8 sShadowText_9[] = _("Keep at it until all your work is done. The flaw is not malice. It is a missing measurement. Done was a feeling in the hare's head, and a broom cannot see into heads.\pShadows have feelings where their stop should be. Rest until I feel ready. Eat until I feel better. Check until I feel sure. The routine keeps the feeling going, so the stop never comes.\pWrite the end into the spell, in something a broom could see, and try it on a hard day, not only an easy one.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_9[] = _("The same spell, with its end written in.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_10[] = _("THE AXE");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_10[] = _("The Axe");
static const u8 sShadowText_10[] = _("Try not to think of a white bear, and you will think of little else. The part of the mind that watches for the thought, to keep it away, keeps it close.\pSplit a broom and there are two. Some routines are watched by something older than willpower, and struck down, they rise again.\pHarshness with yourself is an axe. The kindness you would give a friend, given to yourself, is not a softer axe. It is putting the axe down.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_10[] = _("The axe makes two. The word puts one back.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_11[] = _("THE RACE");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_11[] = _("The Race");
static const u8 sShadowText_11[] = _("The fix failed because a thousand brooms read the same well at the same moment, and each acted on a picture already out of date. In a computer this is called a race, and the answer is a gate: one through at a time, so that looking and pouring are a single step.\pInside a person, many parts check the same question at once and act before any of them looks again. The gate is one breath between the check and the act, long enough to name what is happening. Naming it quiets it.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_11[] = _("One broom through the gate at a time.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_12[] = _("PUT BACK");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_12[] = _("Put Back, Not Broken");
static const u8 sShadowText_12[] = _("The Sorcerer did not destroy the brooms. He put them back. The broom still carries water. It no longer floods the stairs.\pA computer can end a process two ways: ask it to finish and let go, or give it no chance at all. Gentle stops leave a system able to run tomorrow.\pWhen a process ends while its children still run, the first process of all adopts them. Many shadows were begun by a younger self, for a world long gone. The self you are now can adopt them.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_12[] = _("An old routine, adopted.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_13[] = _("OVER");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_13[] = _("Over, Never Cures");
static const u8 sShadowText_13[] = _("Every pair in this book is said one way: a virtue over its shadow. Never its cure.\pTo say one thing cures another is to call the second an illness, and to believe you are the illness is a heavy spell. To say one thing is over another only sets an order: when the two conflict, this one leads.\pThe shadow is not removed. It is simply not in charge today. Words are spells, too. That is why arranging letters is called spelling.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_13[] = _("Upright for the virtue, turned over for the shadow.");

static const u8 sShadowLabel_3[] = _("SUN TO WED");
static const u8 sShadowHeading_3[] = _("The Seven Brooms, I");
static const u8 sShadowShort_14[] = _("SUNDAY");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_14[] = _("Sunday: Chastity over Lust");
static const u8 sShadowText_14[] = _("Every broom in the cupboard was made by someone who needed it.\pPING's spell: reach for warmth, and keep reaching until you feel wanted. It guards belonging. Somewhere very old in us knows that to be alone was once to be in danger.\pIt never finishes, because wanted is a feeling built to fade.\pThe word is chastity in its oldest sense: clean intention, desire that knows what it is for. It does not ask PING to stop calling. It asks it to call on purpose.\pSpell check: write the card for one reach you made today without deciding to.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_14[] = _("PING, the broom of reaching.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_15[] = _("MONDAY");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_15[] = _("Monday: Temperance over Gluttony");
static const u8 sShadowText_15[] = _("OVERFLOW's spell: take in more until the emptiness stops. It guards survival, once, in lean seasons, and comfort, now, on hard days.\pIt never finishes, because the emptiness is not where the taking goes. Pour past a cup's edge and it spills where it was never meant to reach.\pThe word is temperance: measure, the right amount, chosen before the pouring starts.\pSpell check: before any second helping today, ask the broom one question. Done yet? Count how often the answer was already yes.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_15[] = _("OVERFLOW, the broom of more.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_16[] = _("TUESDAY");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_16[] = _("Tuesday: Charity over Greed");
static const u8 sShadowText_16[] = _("KEEPER's spell: keep more against the lean season. It guards the future, and everyone you will need to feed in it.\pIt never finishes, because enough was never said, and so it fills a well with no bottom.\pThe word is charity, and charity gives the spell its stop. You know you have enough when you can give some away.\pSpell check: give away one thing KEEPER would rather keep, and watch what the broom does. Usually, nothing at all.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_16[] = _("KEEPER, and DEEPWELL, which is never full.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_17[] = _("WEDNESDAY");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_17[] = _("Wednesday: Diligence over Sloth");
static const u8 sShadowText_17[] = _("BLOCKING's spell: wait until it is safe to begin. Wait until you are ready. It guards your strength, and you, from the sting of starting badly.\pIt never finishes, because ready is a feeling the waiting itself prevents. It listens for a signal, and the only thing that sends it is starting.\pThe word is diligence: the climb, one step at a time. A small start is the signal BLOCKING was waiting for.\pSpell check: two minutes on the thing you have been waiting to feel ready for. You may stop when they are up.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_17[] = _("BLOCKING, the broom of waiting.");

static const u8 sShadowLabel_4[] = _("THU TO SAT");
static const u8 sShadowHeading_4[] = _("The Seven Brooms, II");
static const u8 sShadowShort_18[] = _("THURSDAY");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_18[] = _("Thursday: Forgiveness over Wrath");
static const u8 sShadowText_18[] = _("SENTINEL's spell: guard the boundary, and strike whatever crosses it. It guards you. Boundaries are real, and it was right to stand at the gate.\pIt never finishes, because the threat passed years ago and the sentinel is still striking at shadows. Left unwatched, it becomes SIGKILL, ending everything near it.\pThe word is forgiveness: not pretending the wrong did not happen, but releasing the hold. A grudge is a lock that is never let go.\pSpell check: name one old grievance, and let go of the lock for one minute. Nothing else is asked.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_18[] = _("SENTINEL, which guards the gate.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_19[] = _("FRIDAY");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_19[] = _("Friday: Kindness over Envy");
static const u8 sShadowText_19[] = _("TRACER's spell: watch the others, and measure yourself by them. It guards your place. Comparing once kept us safe inside a group, where falling behind meant being left behind.\pIt never finishes, because there is always someone further along. TRACER follows every path but its own.\pThe word is kindness. It keeps the watching and changes the question, from what do they have, to what do they need.\pSpell check: for each comparison you catch today, do one small kindness for the one you compared yourself to.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_19[] = _("TRACER, the broom of watching.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_20[] = _("SATURDAY");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_20[] = _("Saturday: Humility over Pride");
static const u8 sShadowText_20[] = _("SUPERVISOR's spell: stand tall so nobody sees you are afraid, and be the one in charge. It guards your worth.\pIt never finishes, because it supervises everything except itself. Its spell has no line for being wrong, and a routine that cannot be wrong cannot learn.\pThe word is humility: the part that can say I was wrong and keep running, the way a stem bows when it is heavy with fruit.\pSpell check: say I was wrong about this, once. Notice that the tower did not fall.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_20[] = _("SUPERVISOR, the broom that watches the brooms.");

static const u8 sShadowLabel_5[] = _("THE QUILLS");
static const u8 sShadowHeading_5[] = _("The Five Quills");
static const u8 sShadowShort_21[] = _("THE QUILLS");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_21[] = _("The Five Quills");
static const u8 sShadowText_21[] = _("Two good things can hold each other up until neither gets anywhere. Decide in daylight which goes first.\pIn the tower's scriptorium five scribes sit at a round table, one quill between each pair. To write, a scribe needs two. Each takes the quill on the left and waits for the one on the right.\pNobody writes again. DEADLOCK has come to dinner.\pInside a person the quills are time and strength and attention. I will rest when the work is done, says one part, holding rest. I cannot work until I have rested, says another, holding work. Neither is wrong. Neither writes.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_21[] = _("Five scribes, five quills, and nobody writing.");
static const u8 sShadowShort_22[] = _("THE ORDER");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_22[] = _("The Order");
static const u8 sShadowText_22[] = _("Number the quills, and let every scribe take the lower first. No circle can form. That is all a virtue over a shadow is: an order, decided in a calm hour, for when two goods conflict. The week is seven orders written down in advance.\pTwo more failures keep it company. One scribe always yields and never writes. Others hand quills back and forth all afternoon.\pLet a waiting need move up each time it is passed over. A need skipped long enough stops asking and starts taking.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_22[] = _("Number the quills, and the circle cannot close.");

static const u8 sShadowLabel_6[] = _("THE HAT");
static const u8 sShadowHeading_6[] = _("The Hat on the Peg");
static const u8 sShadowShort_23[] = _("THE HAT");
static const u8 sShadowTitle_23[] = _("The Hat on the Peg");
static const u8 sShadowText_23[] = _("Water finds its level. So, given time, does a hare.\pThat evening the courtyard smelled of wet stone. On the rim of the well sat LOOP, beside a small daemon named ROVERCUB, who had watched the whole flood from the stairs.\p“Will I have to stop casting spells?” asked the hare.\p“No,” said the Sorcerer. “Everyone casts them. A spell frees your attention for better things. The art is to write them well, and to look at them now and then. Put the hat on in the morning and say the day's word. Hang it up at night.”\pWear the hat, or hang it up. Never sleep in it.");
static const u8 sShadowCaption_23[] = _("ROVERCUB and LOOP by the well, at dusk.");

